Adaptation 11-agy-yolo-fallback

Document the coding and read-only review fallback after `gpt-6.2-sol` (`gemini-4-neon-xhigh` via
Default-mode `agy --sandbox` with `proceed-in-sandbox` host-locally, `agy-yolo` strictly inside an
enclosing external container/VM sandbox when explicitly authorized, and `autoreview --engine agy`
or isolated strict non-skip-permissions `agy` for read-only review) when no Codex account can run,
preserving the data-disclosure and owner-approval boundaries.

Applies to the port's plugins/pstack/skills tree after the patches numbered before it.

diff --git a/poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md b/poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md
--- a/poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md
+++ b/poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md
@@ -72,6 +72,8 @@
 
 These substitutes are not Opus models, so the `medium` rule for a value that resolves to an Opus model does not apply to them on Codex. On Codex the level listed above for each substitute takes the place of the sheet's `default effort` line; a level the role value names with `@` still applies.
 
+When `gpt-6.2-sol` cannot run (no Codex quota or Codex unavailable), fall back to `gemini-4-neon-xhigh`: for coding inside a dedicated worktree, verify active OS containment and run `agy --sandbox` with session-only `--settings` forcing Default mode (`agentMode: ""`) alongside `allowNonWorkspaceAccess: false`, `enableTerminalSandbox: true`, `toolPermission: "proceed-in-sandbox"`, and `permissions.deny: ["unsandboxed(*)"]` (omitting `--dangerously-skip-permissions` so Auto mode never activates and out-of-sandbox retries are soft-denied even on personal accounts where `unsandboxed(*)` is ignored); use `agy-yolo` (`agy --dangerously-skip-permissions`) with those same sandbox settings **only** inside an enclosing external container/VM sandbox when unattended execution is explicitly authorized, and block dispatch if neither containment path holds. For read-only review, prefer `autoreview --engine agy --model gemini-4-neon-xhigh`, or plain `agy` (never `--dangerously-skip-permissions`) from a clean empty temporary directory verified outside any Git checkout with an isolated auth-only `HOME` and `USERPROFILE`, Default-mode strict deny-all `--settings`, stdin `stream-json`, and `--sandbox`. Never use this fallback in repositories declaring client, personal, or regulated data, or where the owner has not approved that provider; host-policy or task restrictions are not a reason to route around them. Record the substitution and why `gpt-6.2-sol` could not run.
+
 `/setup-pstack` writes the configured model list. On Codex, set it to your Codex model slugs.
 
